# Introduction

This is the body content. The interesting part of this fixture is the
**synthesised cover page** that renders before it — see
[`coverpage.style.toml`](coverpage.style.toml) for the configuration.

Render with:

```sh
markdoc-pdf \
    --input  examples/coverpage.mdoc \
    --output coverpage.pdf \
    --style  examples/coverpage.style.toml \
    --assets-root examples
```

Frontmatter fields that feed the cover page:

- `title` → the big H1 at the top of page 1
- `description` → the subtitle template (`{description}` resolves to it)
- `authors` → the joined authors line
- `firstReleaseDate` → the publication-date line
